  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>

  <name>Numo</name>
  <summary>Mental math training</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Numo is an app designed to train mental arithmetic skills.
      Tasks appear one after another, answers are checked immediately, and nothing distracts you.
      Choose from four game modes, select a preset difficulty level, or create a custom configuration.
    </p>

    <p>Pick one of four modes depending on what you want to train:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <em>Survival</em>: an endless run of tasks that ends the moment
        you make a mistake. A test of focus and consistency.
      </li>
      <li>
        <em>Timer</em>: a fixed countdown. Solve as many tasks as you can
        before time runs out.
      </li>
      <li>
        <em>Timer + Bonus</em>: start with a small amount of time and
        earn extra seconds for every correct answer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <em>Task Count</em>: a set number of tasks to solve. A clear goal to
        reach at your own pace.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Three difficulty levels allow you to start with something simple and
      gradually move on to greater challenges.
      In addition, in custom mode, you can adjust the difficulty as you see fit.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <em>Easy</em>: addition, subtraction, and a bit of multiplication.
        Simple operations using small numbers, with no negative numbers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <em>Medium</em>: precise division is introduced. Numbers become larger,
        problems more complex, and addition and subtraction operations may
        involve negative values.
      </li>
      <li>
        <em>Hard</em>: integer division and mod are introduced, and negative
        numbers may now appear in multiplication and division operations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <em>Custom</em>: Complete control over the task.
        Choose any combination of operations, set custom number ranges for each.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Every session is recorded: result, accuracy, and time spent.
      The statistics screen shows your best results per mode and difficulty, recent games.
      The number of recent sessions shown is adjustable.
      Data can be exported and imported as JSON at any time.
    </p>

    <p>
      Numo stays out of your way: large readable tasks, a clean interface,
      and nothing between you and the numbers.
    </p>
  </description>

